// Auto-generated from legacy HTML by scripts/extract-pages.py
export const title = "Counter Event Action Setup Example";
export const html = "<h1>Counter Event Action Setup Example</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n      <p>You can set up events based on a configured counter's values and create action rules.</p>\n      <p>Each counter app includes a separate menu for configuring rules.</p>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-window\">\n  <div class=\"app-main\" style=\"padding:0;\">\n    <div class=\"app-breadcrumb\" style=\"padding:14px 18px 0;\">Home / Application / Occupancy Counting / Event-Action</div>\n    <div class=\"app-h\" style=\"padding:0 18px;\">Event-Action</div>\n    <div style=\"padding:0 18px;display:flex;gap:8px;margin-bottom:10px;\">\n      <span class=\"btn small\">Counter</span><span class=\"btn small primary\">Event-Action</span><span class=\"btn small\">Report</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"app-panel\" style=\"margin:0 18px 18px;\"><strong style=\"font-size:12.5px;\">Event-Action Rules</strong></div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Occupancy Counting &rarr; Event-Action tab</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n      <p>Click the button at the top right of the rule list to add a new counter rule.</p>\n      <div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:170px;\"><span class=\"btn small primary\">+ Add Rule</span></div>\n\n      <h2>Basic Event Action Rule Settings</h2>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:90px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Rule Name</span><input value=\"Rule #8516\" disabled>\n    <span>&#9432; Enable</span><span style=\"background:#2653d6;border-radius:10px;width:34px;height:18px;display:inline-block;position:relative;\"><span style=\"position:absolute;right:2px;top:2px;width:14px;height:14px;background:#fff;border-radius:50%;\"></span></span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n      <ol>\n        <li>Enter a name in <strong>Rule Name</strong> to distinguish this rule. A random default value is pre-filled \u2014 edit it if needed.</li>\n        <li>When configuring the action handler, you can use the <code>{{RULE NAME}}</code> token in the action message to reference the name you set for the rule.</li>\n        <li>If you want the event action rule to be active as soon as it's created, turn on the <strong>Enable</strong> switch.</li>\n      </ol>\n\n      <h2>Event Settings</h2>\n      <p>Click the Add button to configure an event.</p>\n      <p>Select the channel to display the event widget on, and set the widget's position. The channel where the event fires is also set to the channel where the widget is displayed.</p>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\" style=\"max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;\">\n  <div class=\"modal-head\">Event Settings <span>&times;</span></div>\n  <div class=\"modal-body\">\n    <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:90px 1fr 90px;margin-bottom:10px;\">\n      <span>Event Type</span><input value=\"Occupancy Counting\" disabled>\n      <span></span>\n      <span></span><select disabled style=\"outline:2px solid #d64545;\"><option>CH 1</option><option>CH 2</option><option>CH 3</option><option>CH 4</option><option>CH 5</option><option>CH 6</option><option>CH 7</option></select>\n      <span class=\"btn small primary\">+ Add Item</span>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"height:200px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#4a5568,#2d3748);border-radius:6px;\"></div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Selecting the channel to display the event widget on</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n      <p>Assign the target counter for the event under Counter. If there are counters configured in the counter app, they appear in the list.</p>\n      \n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:70px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\"><span>Counter</span><select disabled><option>In-Store People Count</option></select></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n      <p><strong>Event Type</strong> comes in two forms.</p>\n      <ul class=\"steps\">\n        <li><strong>On condition met</strong> &ndash; fires when the specified counter's count value meets a set condition.\n          <ul class=\"steps\">\n            <li><strong>Every N counts</strong> &ndash; fires an event each time the counter's count value crosses a multiple of N, either exceeding it or falling below it. For example, if N=10, an event fires when the count changes from 9 to 10, from 19 to 20, or from 10 back to 9, and so on.</li>\n            <li>If you add a range condition such as greater-than/less-than to the every-N-counts condition, the event does not fire on crossing an N boundary if doing so would violate the range condition.\n              <ul class=\"steps\">\n                <li>If the \"greater than\" value is larger than the \"less than\" value &ndash; the event fires when either condition alone is satisfied. e.g. for X&gt;10, X&lt;5, the event fires when \"X&gt;10 OR X&lt;5\" is true.</li>\n                <li>If the \"greater than\" value is smaller than the \"less than\" value &ndash; the event only fires when both conditions are satisfied. e.g. for 5&lt;X&lt;10, the event fires when \"X&gt;5 AND X&lt;10\" is true.</li>\n                <li><strong>Greater than</strong> &ndash; fires the moment the counter's count value exceeds the configured value.</li>\n                <li><strong>Less than</strong> &ndash; fires the moment the counter's count value falls below the configured value.</li>\n                <li>The greater-than and less-than events are independent of each other, so there's no requirement that one value be larger than the other &mdash; the event fires whenever the count rises above or falls below whichever value you configured.</li>\n              </ul>\n            </li>\n          </ul>\n        </li>\n        <li><strong>On every interval</strong> &ndash; fires a count event at a fixed time interval.\n          <ul class=\"steps\">\n            <li>The event fires at the configured interval.</li>\n            <li>If you add a range condition such as greater-than/less-than to the every-interval condition, the range condition behaves the same way as described above for the every-N-counts setting.</li>\n          </ul>\n        </li>\n      </ul>\n\n      <h2>Action Settings</h2>\n      <p>The action settings define what happens when the configured event occurs.</p>\n      <p>Click the Add button to add a new action item.</p>\n      <p>For the supported action types and how to configure them, see the <a href=\"#\">Action Setting Guide</a>. Configure each action you want to run when the event occurs.</p>\n\n      <h2>Finishing Setup</h2>\n      <p>Once you've finished configuring the event and action settings for the rule set, click the button at the bottom to submit the event action settings.</p>\n      <p>If the settings were applied successfully, you can see the item in the list on the counter action rule screen.</p>\n\n      <h2>Filter Settings (Optional)</h2>\n      <p>You can use schedule and combined-rule filters to configure event filters that gate whether an action runs. The schedule and combined-rule filter settings described below are not required to build an action rule &mdash; configure them only if needed.</p>\n\n      <h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">Schedule Settings</h3>\n      <p>You can configure an event action schedule. Schedules run on a recurring basis and are used to set the time window in which an action should run when an event occurs.</p>\n      <ol>\n        <li>Click the button to configure an event action schedule.</li>\n        <li>For detailed instructions, see the <a href=\"#\">Schedule Setting Guide</a>. Add a schedule setting to gate when actions run in response to events.</li>\n      </ol>\n\n      <h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">Combined Rule Condition Settings</h3>\n      <ol>\n        <li>You can add combined conditions to event actions to perform more sophisticated event filtering. The items you can use as combined conditions are:\n          <ul class=\"steps\">\n            <li>Rules configured on event-action-type applications</li>\n            <li>Events that make up rules configured on event-action-type applications</li>\n            <li>System I/O devices such as Alarm In or Virtual Alarm In</li>\n          </ul>\n        </li>\n        <li>Click the Add button to configure a combined rule condition.</li>\n        <li>For detailed instructions, see the <a href=\"#\">Combined Rule Condition Setting Guide</a>.</li>\n      </ol>";
